== room | LATE NIGHT · CHIDI'S ROOM | dark bedroom late at night lit by a laptop screen and a small lamp | phone
chidi (cheer): Quddus! I finished my scholarship essay in two minutes. AI wrote it. It's beautiful.
quddus (think): Read me the first line.
chidi (talk): Ever since I was a child in the vibrant streets of my city, my passion for innovation has burned like a thousand suns.
quddus (facepalm): Chidi. A thousand suns? The committee has read that sun many times.

== cafe | NEXT DAY · CAFÉ | calm café with soft lights, plants and a notebook on the table | cafe +laptop
chidi (worried): So I can't use AI at all?
quddus (talk): Use it as a helper, not as the writer. Brainstorm ideas, check grammar, or ask it what's unclear. But the story and the facts must be yours.
> 1f916 | USING AI WISELY | 2705 Brainstorm + grammar checks | 1f4dd Your real stories and facts | 1f4cb Follow each program's AI rules
chidi (think): What if they check?
quddus (point): Some programs ban AI-written essays. And generic text is easy to spot. Your real experience is what makes you stand out.
chidi (cheer): New first line: in my final year, I fixed my school's broken water pump with a phone charger. True story!
